  "title": "fix(ui): orthographic depth maps into WebGPU's clip volume, not OpenGL's",
  "user": {
    "login": "tbrasselle",
    "id": 4564956,
    "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NjQ5NTY=",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4564956?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/tbrasselle",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/tbrasselle",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/tbrasselle/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/tbrasselle/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/tbrasselle/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/tbrasselle/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/tbrasselle/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/tbrasselle/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/tbrasselle/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/tbrasselle/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/tbrasselle/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "The ortho branch of `Camera::mvp` mapped depth the way OpenGL's `glOrtho` does - NDC z over [-1, +1]. WebGPU's clip volume wants `0 <= z <= w`, and the ortho matrix holds `clip.w == 1` (the #434 law tests pin that), so every point nearer than `(near + far) / 2` was clipped away before rasterization. With `far = 40 * dist`, that cut plane sits twenty times the orbit distance out: everything in view, so clicking **Orthographic** blanked the viewport.\n\nPerspective carries the same OpenGL-style z row but `clip.w` is the eye distance there, which keeps clip z positive beyond ~0.2 mm - far closer than the camera can orbit - so perspective was unaffected.\n\n## The change\n\nThe ortho z row (`viewport.rs`, the `[col][row]` proj literal) becomes\n\n```rust\n[0.0, 0.0, 1.0 / (near - far), 0.0],\n[0.0, 0.0, near / (near - far), 1.0],\n```\n\nnear maps to 0.0, far to 1.0, and ortho depth is now linear. The depth attachment already clears to 1.0 under `CompareFunction::Less`, so no pipeline or shader change is needed. The x/y rows already speak WebGPU and are untouched, as is the perspective branch (its z quirk costs depth precision, not geometry - out of scope here).\n\n## Pins (red on main, green with the fix)\n\n- `law_tests::projection_tests::the_ortho_depth_spans_zero_to_one_between_the_planes` - depth at the near plane, the far plane, and strictly between with monotonic climb. On main: \"the near plane sits at -1\".\n- `gpu_render::orthographic_paints_the_band_perspective_does` - the stock box from `box_stock_paints_steel_over_background` under `test_cam()`, painted in both modes, with the same band bounds and a comparability check (each within 1.5x of the other). On main: 0/65536 pixels.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --no-run` builds clean.\n- `camcraft-ui --lib`: 378 passed, 5 ignored.\n- `--test gpu_render`: 10 passed (9 existing + the new one).\n- `--test trace_composite`: 4 passed (its first run hit the known pre-existing fallback-device crash race; clean on rerun, and it only exercises the untouched perspective path).\n\nChangelog: orthographic view no longer blanks the viewport - the parallel depth row maps into WebGPU's clip volume (#600)\n\nFixes #600\n",
